# Mac Studio (M4 Max), the llama.cpp text cells on the b11721 pin (owner decision 2026-10-19: the comparison arms are
# measured on their current release too; llama.cpp b8999 -> b11721, environment.lock.json arms.llama.cpp since
# 2026-10-19). The session anchor row, then the ten llama.cpp rows, each byte-identical to its source line
# (cooldown and context-tokens unchanged).
# Source: matrices/dashboard-text-v1.cells line 199 (anchor) and lines 201, 207, 214, 220, 227, 233, 240, 246, 253, 259
# (short-chat and long-context-1024-gen256 of Qwen3 0.6B / 1.7B / 4B and Gemma 4 E2B / E4B).
# Needs the yardstick built on the b11721 xcframework (Vendored/llama.xcframework + its .tag, then
# scripts/build_yardstick_mac.sh): its records stamp engineVersion b11721, engineArtifact llama-b11721-xcframework.zip.
# Run through the job route in a Mac window (no heavy export pipeline; the job runs anchors.cells, admits, posts):
#   python3 scripts/dashboard_job.py m4max --cells matrices/dashboard-llama-b11721-mac.cells --suffix llama-b11721 --once

# ---- mac ----
mac mlx-swift mlx-community/Qwen3-0.6B-4bit short-chat anchor=1 runs=3
mac llama.cpp unsloth/Qwen3-0.6B-GGUF/Q4_K_M short-chat
mac llama.cpp unsloth/Qwen3-0.6B-GGUF/Q4_K_M long-context-1024-gen256 context-tokens=2048
mac llama.cpp unsloth/Qwen3-1.7B-GGUF/Q4_K_M short-chat
mac llama.cpp unsloth/Qwen3-1.7B-GGUF/Q4_K_M long-context-1024-gen256 context-tokens=2048
